<title>GERMANY: German ZEW details 6-mth major nations forecasts.</title>
<headline>German ZEW details 6-mth major nations forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>MANNHEIM, Germany 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table lists the economic and market forecasts for the six months from December 18 issued by the ZEW Zentrum fuer Europaeische Wirtschaftsforschung GmbH research institute. The averages are compiled from a survey of 299 firms conducted from December 2 to 17.</p>
<p>					  Base    Forecast</p>
<p>INFLATION RATES</p>
<p>    Germany			    1.4     1.5</p>
<p>    U.S.				 3.3     3.5</p>
<p>    Japan				0.1     0.3</p>
<p>    Britain			    2.7     2.9</p>
<p>    France			     1.6     1.7</p>
<p>    Italy				2.6     2.6</p>
<p>SHORT-TERM RATES (Three-month interbank rates)</p>
<p>    Germany			    3.2     3.3</p>
<p>    U.S.				 4.9     5.3</p>
<p>    Japan				0.5     0.8</p>
<p>    Britain			    6.3     6.7</p>
<p>    France			     3.5     3.6</p>
<p>    Italy				7.1     7.1</p>
<p>LONG-TERM RATES</p>
<p>    Germany			    5.8     6.1</p>
<p>    U.S.				 6.3     6.8</p>
<p>    Japan				2.5     2.8</p>
<p>    Britain			    7.6     7.9</p>
<p>    France			     5.8     6.0</p>
<p>    Italy				7.6     7.8</p>
<p>BOURSE</p>
<p>    German DAX		     2,850   2,910</p>
<p>    U.S. Dow Jones		 6,370   6,330</p>
<p>    Japan Nikkei		  20,600  21,200</p>
<p>    Britain FT-SE 100	    4,010   4,000</p>
<p>    France CAC-40		  2,250   2,330</p>
<p>    Italy MIBtel		  10,300  10,700</p>
<p>EXCHANGE RATES VS MARK</p>
<p>    Swiss franc		     1.18    1.16</p>
<p>    U.S. dollar		     1.55    1.62</p>
<p>    Japanese yen		    1.37    1.38</p>
<p>    British pound		   2.57    2.59</p>
<p>    French franc		    2.96    2.95</p>
<p>    Italian lira		    1.02    1.01</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
